jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.6.0~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. Neither storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * Adds the dellpowervault storage type for PowerVault ME4 and ME5.
  * The ME series exposes its CLI over HTTPS rather than a REST object model,
    so HTTP 200 does not mean success: every command is judged by the CLI's
    own status object instead.
  * expand volume takes the amount to ADD, while PVE asks for the new total,
    so the delta is computed by the plugin.
  * Sizes are rounded UP to the array's 4 MiB granularity, because the array
    rounds down and would return a volume smaller than requested.
  * Names on this family are limited to 32 bytes and may not contain a dot,
    which is why it has its own naming module and a 10-character budget for
    the storage id. A name that would not fit is an error, not a silent
    truncation that could collide with another VM's volume.
  * Verified on a live PVE node that both Dell plugins load together without
    the duplicate-property failure that would take down every storage.

 -- Jason Cheng (Jason Tools) <jason@jason.tools>  Sun, 26 Jul 2026 23:00:00 +0800

jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.5.0~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. See the disclaimer in README.md:
    this has never been run against a physical Dell EMC array, a defect can
    destroy VM data or hang a node, and there is no warranty of any kind.
  * Phases 2 to 4: the dellpowerstore storage type now exists. It has NOT
    been run against a PowerStore array - see docs/TESTING.md, where every
    array-facing detail is still listed as unverified.
  * Common::BlockBase: the abstract PVE plugin base. Activation, allocation,
    device discovery and teardown, snapshots, templates, clones, the
    multipath drop-in and the background orphan reaper, all independent of
    which array is behind them.
  * PowerStore::API: REST client for volumes, snapshots, thin clones, hosts,
    mappings and the transport endpoints. Listing filters server-side and
    follows pages; LUN ids are assigned by the client rather than by the
    array, because PowerStore's REST-side sequence starts at 200 and never
    reuses an id.
  * DellPowerStorePlugin: the storage type itself.
  * bin/pve-dell-config-get: reads a VM configuration back out of the config
    backup volume written alongside each snapshot, including in recover mode
    where it talks to the array directly and never touches the PVE stack.
  * Documentation: quick start, configuration reference, architecture,
    troubleshooting, naming conventions and the hardware test matrix, all in
    English and Traditional Chinese, plus the project page under docs/.
  * 713 unit tests, none of which need an array or a device.

 -- Jason Cheng (Jason Tools) <jason@jason.tools>  Sun, 26 Jul 2026 19:00:00 +0800

jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Phase 1: the shared Common layer. Still no PVE storage type — these are
    the modules the plugins will be built on.
  * Naming: object naming and the pve-<storeid>- ownership gate that guards
    every destructive path.
  * REST: HTTP transport with the retry policy the health path depends on —
    a POST is never retried on 5xx, 401 re-authenticates once, 429/503 back
    off with a capped Retry-After.
  * Multipath: dm-multipath and SCSI device lifecycle, ported from the
    NetApp and Pure plugins with the vendor gate parameterised. Every sysfs
    access is timeout-bounded and the system-wide flush cannot be reached.
  * ISCSI: initiator, portal probing and per-session rescan.
  * FC: HBA WWPN discovery and WWN normalisation. Does not issue a LIP by
    default.
  * WwidState: per-node WWID tracking with the grace period and miss
    threshold the orphan reaper needs before it may tear a device down.
  * Health: outage detection and capacity alerting for status(), rate
    limited so a ~10s poll cannot flood the journal.
  * 342 unit tests across t/01-naming.t .. t/05-state.t.

 -- Jason Cheng (Jason Tools) <jason@jason.tools>  Sun, 26 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0800

jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Phase 0: project skeleton.
  * Packaging: debian/ set, Makefile with install/uninstall/test/deb targets,
    GitHub Actions build workflow.
  * Safety: CI guard that fails the build if the system-wide multipath flush
    (`multipath -F`, capital F, which must never be used) appears anywhere in
    shipped code or documentation.
  * Docs: bilingual README skeleton (English / Traditional Chinese) with the
    multipath safety rules and the hardware-verification disclaimer.
  * No storage plugin code yet — this release installs no PVE storage type.

 -- Jason Cheng (Jason Tools) <jason@jason.tools>  Sun, 26 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0800
